  "_doc": "One row per weave. flows = threads of each Power (their sum is the flow slots the weave occupies while forming or held). book = earliest book (0 = New Spring) and drives the spoiler setting. confidence: canon | wiki | unknown | game | user (see docs/WEAVES.md). flows_saidin = the flows a man uses where they differ. talent = the Talent that makes this weave far stronger and waives its strength gate; nobody needs a Talent to learn a weave. level = weakest Companion strength level that can make it work. form = seconds it takes to weave before it can be loosed (there are no cooldowns: the time is in the making; a weave that is whole can be held back in the hands and aimed). hold = it lasts while you hold it, occupying its flows and costing a little of its draw each second; weaving it again lets it go. kind bind (Bonds of Air) and sever (a shield) fasten on one body: base.hold is how many seconds a strong one takes to break free. on_hit = (charge: lightning leaves survivors running wild for that many seconds, and the next blow sends the charge to two neighbours; daze: Spirit leaves them without purpose) what the weave leaves on those it strikes (burn + burn_dps, stun, down: seconds). self = share of a blast's damage its own weaver takes if caught in it. gravity and loft (in base) make a projectile arc. needs = weaves you must know before you can study this one; study = how much channelling it takes to work it out (halved once you have seen it woven). pierce (in base) = bodies a dart goes through before it stops; dart = drawn as a streak, not a ball. lash: a line that pulls (base.pull) what it reaches toward the weaver; on_hit.wet = seconds soaked (slowed, and lightning hits half again as hard). blossom: a pillar (pillar s, pillar_radius) that opens (open s) into a wheel of fire of radius between radius_min and radius_max by strength, burning (dps) for duration. ring: base.arc = half-angle of the wedge it rolls out in. kind picks the sim behaviour; base holds its numbers at reference power 10.",
